{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>From that land went out Asshur.</b> He was of the sons of Shem, as it says, ״בני שם עילם ואשור״ — the sons of Shem: Elam and Asshur. And since the generation of the dispersion (dor ha-palagah) was mostly from the sons of Shem, therefore Scripture notes of Asshur that he went out from the land — for he was not party to the counsel of the generation of the dispersion, as our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted. And what is written (Psalms 83:9), ״גם אשור נלוה עמהם״ — 'Asshur also is joined with them' — indicates that Asshur did not do evil to Israel like the other nations."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:31.099494733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}